  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 1229 AM MDT Thu Jul 23 2026\n\nFriday...\n\nPrecip coverage will lessen a bit on Friday, with most activity \nstaying over the higher terrain. For the plains, a more stable \nairmass will be in place, allowing for only a few isolated showers \nalong and west of I-25. Meanwhile, scattered to more widespread \nshowers and storms will form by mid-afternoon and last into early \nFriday Night over the peaks of the mountains. Burn scar flash \nflooding will continue to be the primary concern.\n\n\nThis Weekend Onwards...\n\nAs the upper high moves overhead, flow weakens aloft. Forcing for \nstorms will significantly weaken, though recycling monsoon moisture \nwill be plentiful enough to keep afternoon showers and storms going \nover the mountains. Meanwhile, the plains will dry out again, with \ntriple-digit temperatures returning. Current long-range guidance \nsuggests a wetter and potentially cooler (or at least less hot) \npattern as we move into next week.",
